# Verify CodexFlow

Run a read-only health check.

## Check Required Files

- `AGENTS.md`
- `.agents/skills/init-codexflow/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/plan-session/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/start-session/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/checkpoint-session/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/end-session/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/new-feature/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/verify-codexflow/SKILL.md`
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/.codexflow.json`
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/CONFIG.md`
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/ROADMAP.md`
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/SESSION_LOG.md`
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/OVERVIEW.md`
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/ADR.md`
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/CUSTOM.md`
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/LEARNED_PATTERNS.md`

## Check Consistency

- Every roadmap task should have `[feature: name]`.
- Session log entries should include a feature and date.
- `AGENTS.md` should mention the docs path and commands.
- Feature specs in `feature_docs/` should have matching roadmap feature tags when implementation has started.

## Optional Hooks

If `.codex/hooks.json` exists:

- Read it and confirm commands point to `.codex/hooks/`.
- Check hook scripts with `node --check`.
- Remind the user to review hooks with `/hooks` before trusting them.

## Output

Report:

- OK items
- warnings
- missing files
- suggested fixes

Do not modify files.
